Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; No usable D3D12 driver exists here (Dozen is Vulkan 1.2 without what Dawn
; needs; llvmpipe D3D12 compiles too slowly for client handshakes), so make
; D3D12 resolve as absent and let clients fall back cleanly. Revisit when a
; conformant D3D12 driver is available. dxgi/d3d11 stay on DXVK.
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\DllOverrides]
"d3d12"=""
"d3d12core"=""
